<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Life of Antony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 360</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Life of Antony is a biography of the Egyptian hermit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anthony-the-great">Anthony the Great</a>, written in Greek by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athanasius-of-alexandria">Athanasius of Alexandria</a> soon after Anthony's death in 356. It describes his withdrawal into the desert, his struggles with demons and his holiness. Quickly translated into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, it spread the ideal of monastic life across the Christian West and is mentioned by Augustine as a spur to his conversion.</p></div>
